We explored different ML methods to determine which PROMs are most useful for both referral of patients in- and to MBR using dataset 2. We used the clinician’s decision as ground truth. Two classifier algorithms: (1) Balanced Random Forest (RF) classifier [30] and (2) Random Under-sampling Boosting classifier (RUSBoost) [31] were chosen because of their ability to deal with class imbalance, handle small data sets and ease of interpretability. Both algorithms create an ensemble of models with a Decision Tree [32] as base estimator, which is also a classifier that has often been used in related work [33–35]. In addition, the respective classifiers were chosen because of their (1) integrated solution to deal with class imbalance; (2) ability to handle mixed data types; (3) ability to perform well with a small sample size (n \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
